From 641342ae89f69dd30abc24f746ee671da9c097ab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mechres <164776284+Mechres@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 08:29:40 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 10/11] Import ION buffers as plain dma-bufs (SUPPORT_ION +
 PVR_ION_DMABUF_COMPAT)

The stock gralloc maps its ION buffers into the services with MAP_ION_HANDLE.
Mainline has no in-kernel ION; buffers now come from the ion_compat /dev/ion
driver as dma-buf fds. env/linux/ion.c reimplements the DDK's ION import API with
the generic dma-buf API (attach to the SGX device, collect page addresses, vmap the
first plane) and the per-process ION client is skipped. ion_sync.h from the TI
1.14.3699939 tree. All 176 interface structures (now including the ION bridge
structures) still match the stock module. With this the stock Allwinner 1.12 EGL
and GLES2 libraries render correctly through this driver.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
